WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.290
- So hello everyone,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.800
and welcome to "Academic
Jobs Outside the US."

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.610
This is the third and final
webinar in our three-part series

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.120
on Doing Chinese History in a New Era.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.800
The series is organized by
Denise Ho at Yale University,

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.940
and myself, Emily Baum at UC Irvine.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.960
We are very excited to be
broadcasting to you live

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.441
from the same location in
Southern California. Surprise!

00:00:32.441 --> 00:00:35.690
And this webinar series has
been generously sponsored

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.276
by The Council on East Asian
Studies at Yale University

00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:42.540
and the Long US-China
Institute at UC Irvine.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.620
We are also very grateful to
our long list of co-sponsors.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.028
We will just read their names
out very quickly right now.

